{title: Prince of Peace}
{subtitle: Isaiah 9:1–6}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm] [Eb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The people who walked in darkness have seen a great [Ebmaj7/G]light
On those who lived in a land [Eb]of deep shadow, [Bb]light has dawned
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The yoke upon their shoulders [Eb]and the bar ac[Gm]ross their [Eb]back
The rod of the oppres[F]sor lies shattered in its track
Ev[Gm]ery boot that tramped in tumult, [Eb]every cloak rolled in [Bb]blood
Is fuel now for the fire, and [F]joy comes like a flood
They re[Gm]joice as at the harvest when the [Eb]sheaves are carried in
[Bb]The long night is ending and the [F]morning will begin
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
For to [Bb]us a child is born, [F/A]to [Gm]us a son is given
[F]And [Eb]the government will rest on [Bb]his shoul[F]ders
And [Bb]his name shall be called [Gm]Wonderful Counselor
[F]Mighty [Eb]God, Everlasting Fa[F]ther, Prince of [Bb]Peace
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
He will sit on David's throne and over [Eb]all his [Gm]land
With [Eb]justice and with righteousness up[F]held by his hand
From [Gm]now until forever his [Eb]kingdom will not cease
The [Bb]zeal of the LORD of hosts will [F]accomplish this
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
For [Bb]to us a child is born, [F/A]to [Gm]us a son is given
[F]And the [Eb]government will rest on his [Bb]shoul[F]ders
And his [Bb]name shall be called Won[Gm]derful Counselor
[F]Mighty [Eb]God, Everlasting Father, [F]Prince of [Bb]Peace
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Of the [Gm]increase of his government and of [Eb]peace there will be no end
The [Bb]zeal of the LORD of hosts will ac[F]complish this
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Wonderful Counselor, [Gm]Mighty God [F]
[Eb]Everlasting Father, [F]Prince of [Bb]Peace
{end_of_verse}
